\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If $p_n$ is the nth prime, must the set of indices n with $p_{n+1}-p_n>C$ log $p_n$ have positive lower natural density for every fixed $C>0$? The positive density may depend on C.

\subsection{Short English statement}
If $p_n$ is the nth prime, must the set of indices n with $p_{n+1}-p_n>C$ log $p_n$ have positive lower natural density for every fixed $C>0$? The positive density may depend on C.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2008/14}.
\item[S2] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CramerConjecture.html}.
\item[S3] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Positive-lower-density-of-large-prime-gaps-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

